\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 \\rotations=<float,float,float>
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 The rotation angles (in degrees) of the gantry, collimator and table. If no specified
\par rotations remain unchanged.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 \\jaws=<float,float,float,float>
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 The jaws aperture. The order is x1,x2,y1,y2. If no specified the jaws aperture
\par remains unchanged. 
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 \\iso=<float,float,float> 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 The position x,y,z of the isocenter. If this parameter is not specified the isocenter
\par remains unchanged. The isocenter position is changed for all fields in the plan.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 \\mlc=<integer>
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 The code of the MLC to be linked to the field. If not specified the MLC remains
\par unchanged. For available MLC codes use the list command. The MLC is changed  for all
\par fields in the plan.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 \\eappl=<integer>
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 The code of the electron applicator to be linked to the field. If not specified the
\par electron applicator remains unchanged. For the available electron-applicator codes
\par use the list command.
\par 
\par Example: 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf19\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 config.field \\field=1 \\rotations=180,0,0 \\iso=0,0,5.0  
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs22\cf17\insrsid11617927\charrsid1005749 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs24\ul\cf7\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 config.linac
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 This command changes the linac model and linac operating mode of the project. }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid3605984\charrsid1005749 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 This command resets all the project data (including the patient model) to default. }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid3605984\charrsid1005749 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 Also, all simulation results are deleted. Therefore, this command must be used with }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid3605984\charrsid1005749 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 extreme caution. 
\par 
\par Parameters:
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 \\linac=<integer>
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 The linac model code. Default is \\linac=6 which corresponds to a Varian Clinac 2100 C/D. }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid3605984\charrsid1005749 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 To see the available linac codes use the list command.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 \\mode=<integer>
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 The linac operation mode. Accepted values are \\mode=1 and \\mode=2 which corresponds}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid3605984\charrsid1005749 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749  to electron and photon modes, respectively.
\par 
\par Example:
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf19\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 config.linac \\linac=5 \\mode=2
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs24\ul\cf7\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 config.simu 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 Configures the simulation parameters.
\par  
\par Parameters:
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 \\seg=<text> 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 Defines the segment to be configured. Default is \\seg=s1. Accepted values are: s1,
\par s2, s3, s1s2, s1s2s3 and s2s3.
\par  
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 \\engine=<text>
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 Defines the simulation engine. Default is \\engine=penelope. Accepted values are:
\par penelope and dpm
\par  
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 \\coarse: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid809661\charrsid1005749 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 If specified (and the selected engine is DPM), the (coarse) low resolution
\par dose simulation is set.
\par  
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 \\seeds
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 If specified a new sequence of the random number generator is generated.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 \\time=<float>
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 Set the stop condition to be the simulation time in seconds. Default stop condition
\par is by number of histories. This option is only valid when the simulation engine 
\par selected is \\engine=penelope
\par  
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 \\histories=<float>
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 Set the stop condition to the number of histories. 
\par  
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 \\sigma=<float> 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 Set the stop condition to the uncertainty (in %). This option is only valid when
\par the simulation engine is \\engine=penelope and the tally is the dose distribution. 
\par When no stop condition is specified, the stop by number of histories condition is
\par set and the number of histories is taken from the default for the segment to be
\par simulated (10^9 for segment s1 or the total number of histories in the source phase
\par space for other segments).
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 \\refresh=<float>
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 Set the output refresh time in seconds. Default is \\refresh=60. This option is
\par only valid when the simulation engine is \\engine=penelope. 
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 \\cpus=<integer>
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 Set the number of processes used in simulations with PENELOPE. Default is \\cpus=1. 
\par 
\par Example: 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf19\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 config.simu \\seg=s1 \\engine=penelope \\time=3600 \\histories=10000000 \\cpus=8  
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs24\ul\cf7\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 config.vr 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 Configures the variance-reduction techniques.
\par 
\par Parameters:
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 \\force=<integer>
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 Activates interaction forcing in the linac target. 
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 \\rotational 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 Activates rotational splitting (with the option `fitted') in the simulation of
\par segment s1. 
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 \\rotationalfull
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 Activates rotational splitting (with the option `biggest') in the simulation of
\par segment s1. 
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 \\roulette
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 Activates splitting roulette (with the option `fitted') in the simulation of
\par segment s1. 
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 \\roulettefull
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 Activates splitting roulette (with the option `biggest') in the simulation of
\par segment s1. 
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 \\split=<integer>
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 Activates simple splitting in phantom or CT in the simulation of segment s3. 
\par 
\par Example: 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf19\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 config.vr \\split=300   
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs24\ul\cf7\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 gamma 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 Performs a comparison by gamma analysis of the project dose distribution with
\par an external dose distribution.
\par 
\par Parameters:
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 \\primo 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 The external dose is expected to be primo formatted and will be search for in
\par the PRIMO repository. Default is \\dpm.
\par  
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 \\deltadose=<float>
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 The dose difference criterion in percentage. Default is 3.0%.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 \\dta=<float>
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 The distance-to-agreement criterion in centimeters. Default is 0.3 cm.
\par  
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 \\threshold=<float>
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 The dose threshold in percentage. Only dose values greater than this threshold
\par will be considered in agamma analysis. Default is 10% of the maximum reference dose.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 \\unc=<float>
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 The uncertainty lower limit in percentage. All those voxels of the reference dose
\par distribution with uncertainty larger than the specified value will be not included
\par in gamma analysis. Default is 100%.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 \\region=<text>
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 The ID of a structure. Only those voxels inside this region will be considered in
\par the analysis. }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid11617927\charrsid1005749 Typically,}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749  \\region=body. By }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid11617927\charrsid1005749 default,}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749  the analysis is performed in the
\par whole dose distribution.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 \\ref=<text>
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 Sets the reference dose. By }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid11617927\charrsid1005749 default,}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749  the reference dose is the project dose.
\par Set this parameters to \\ref=external to force the reference dose to be the
\par imported dose.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid11617927\charrsid1005749 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid11617927\charrsid1005749 \\local
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid11617927\charrsid1005749 Activates local analysis. Dose difference is compared with the specified percentage of
\par  the local reference dose. By default, the analysis is global, that is the dose difference}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid11617927\charrsid1005749 is compared with the specified percentage of the global dose maximum.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid11617927 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid4412499 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf22\insrsid4412499\charrsid4741915 \\smooth=<text> 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid4412499\charrsid4412499 Smooths the dose distribution previous to gamma analysis. Possible values are: ref to}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid4741915 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid4412499\charrsid4412499 smooth the reference dose when it is the Monte Carlo estimated dose of the project; }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid4741915 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid4412499\charrsid4412499 both to smooth both dose distributions, the internal and external provided they both}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid4741915 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid4412499\charrsid4412499 are Monte Carlo estimated dose }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid4741915\charrsid4412499 distributions}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid4741915 .}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid4412499\charrsid4412499  The dose imported in DICOM format is}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid4741915 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid4412499\charrsid4412499 never smoothed. If the parameter }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid4412499 \\}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid4412499\charrsid4412499 
ref=external is employed, using \\smooth=ref will}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid4741915 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid4412499\charrsid4412499 have no effect whatsoever. In this case use \\smooth=both to smooth the non-reference}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid4741915 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid4412499\charrsid4412499 project dose distribution.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid4412499\charrsid1005749 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 Example: 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf19\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 gamma \\deltadose=2.0 \\dta=0.2 \\region=body \\ref=external  
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs24\ul\cf7\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 get.env 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 Outputs the paths of the DICOM and PRIMO repositories.
\par 
\par Parameters:
\par None
\par 
\par Example: 
\par get.env  
\par 
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs24\ul\cf7\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 import.ct 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 Imports DICOM-CT files. 
\par 
\par Requirements:
\par The CT files are searched for in the DICOM repository with the search mask CT*.dcm
\par 
\par Parameters:
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 \\reduce
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 If specified, this parameter force to reduce the size of the CT volume. Otherwise
\par the CT volume is imported in its original size.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 \\segment
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 If specified, this parameter force to create the simulation geometry by segmenting
\par the CT volume after import. Otherwise the simulation geometry is not created. 
\par 
\par Example: 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf19\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 import.ct \\reduce \\segment  
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs24\ul\cf7\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 import.dynalogs 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 Reconstructs the plan from the dynalog files.
\par 
\par Requirements:
\par The dynalog files are searched for in the DICOM repository with the search
\par mask *.dlg
\par 
\par Parameters:
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 \\uniform
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \f41\fs20\cf17\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 Forces uniform sampling.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs20\cf21\insrsid2451147\charrsid1005749 \\timeres=<float>
